  "task_description": "{'component_name': 'Main Container for TransitPulse India', 'description': 'Primary container for TransitPulse India implementation: TransitPulse India is a mobile app designed to help users track and plan public transportation across major Indian cities. It integrates real-time and schedule data for buses and metros, provides walking directions to stops, supports trip planning, and offers offline access to previously viewed routes. The app features a clean, minimal UI with multi-language support and is optimized for low-end Android devices.', 'interfaces': [], 'framework': 'react', 'platform': 'web', 'container': '{\n  "name": "TransitPulse India-39017 frontend Container",\n  "features": [\n    {\n      "name": "Map View with Nearby Stops",\n      "description": "Displays user\'s current location and nearby bus/metro stops using OpenStreetMap or Mapbox. Real-time map markers for selected routes and stops.",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "GTFS Integration",\n      "description": "Fetches and displays bus and metro routes and schedules for Indian cities using GTFS feeds from data.gov.in.",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "Walking Directions",\n      "description": "Calculates walking routes to the nearest bus/metro stop using OpenRouteService API.",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "Trip Planner",\n      "description": "Combines walking and public transport routes using schedule data to help users plan trips efficiently.",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "Search & ETAs",\n      "description": "Allows users to search for stops, view estimated arrival times, and see lists of arriving buses or metro trains.",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "Multi-language Support",\n      "description": "Supports English and Hindi for the app interface, with potential for more languages in the future.",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "Offline Access",\n      "description": "Enables offline access to previously viewed routes and schedules using local storage or SQLite.",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "Crowd-sourced Reports",\n      "description": "Allows users to report bus delays and crowd levels via Firebase or Supabase (optional feature).",\n      "isEnabled": false\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "Location Permissions Handling",\n      "description": "Smoothly manages location permissions to ensure seamless user experience.",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    }\n  ],\n  "techStack": {\n    "frontend": [\n      "React JS"\n    ],\n    "backend": [\n      "None"\n    ],\n    "language": [\n      "JavaScript (ES6+)"\n    ]\n  },\n  "colors": {\n    "primary": "#1976D2",\n    "secondary": "#FFFFFF",\n    "accent": "#FFC107"\n  },\n  "theme": "light",\n  "layoutDescription": "The app uses a bottom navigation bar with four main tabs: \'Nearby Stops\', \'Plan Trip\', \'Saved Routes\', and \'My City\'. The main screen features a clean map view with minimal overlays, real-time markers, and a search bar. Each section is designed for quick access and minimal clutter, optimized for low-end devices."\n}'}",
